## Open PR

1. Go to: https://github.com/raghuchandra22/psin-enconnexerp
2. Yellow banner → **Compare & pull request**
3. ⚠️ **Base branch: `Sandbox-18`** (NOT `main`)
4. Title:
   ```
   Add Flat Partner Report Export wizard
   ```
5. Description:
   ```
   ## What
   New wizard under Accounting → Reporting menu that exports Partner Ledger,
   Aged Receivable, and Aged Payable to Excel with a dedicated "Partner Name"
   column on the left.

   ## Why
   Default XLSX export shows partner name only as a section header, not as
   a column value. That makes the file hard to use for pivot tables,
   filtering by partner, or any data analysis. This wizard solves that.

   ## How it works
   - Wizard accepts: report type, date range, optional company
   - Calls Odoo's native `account.report.export_to_xlsx(options)` so column
     structure, aging buckets, and totals match the standard reports exactly
   - Post-processes the file: inserts Partner Name column, tags every row,
     removes section-header separator rows
   - Existing PDF/XLSX exports completely untouched

   ## Reports supported
   - Partner Ledger
   - Aged Receivable
   - Aged Payable

   ## Tested locally
   - All 3 reports export correctly
   - Partner Name appears on every transaction row
   - Initial Balance rows preserved with partner tagged
   - Numbers/totals match the native reports

   ## Note for reviewer
   While working on this, I noticed `models/account_report.py` contains
   legacy Odoo 14 API code (`account.aged.payable`, `account.aged.receivable`)
   that fails to load in Odoo 18 — the model `account.aged.payable` doesn't
   exist anymore. I disabled the import in `models/__init__.py` so the
   registry can load. The file is preserved on disk. Cleanup of that legacy
   file can be done in a separate task if you'd like.
   ```
6. Request senior review
